CHECK:COMPARISON_TO_NULL: Comparison to NULL could be written "!ins"
#62: FILE: sound/pci/cs46xx/dsp_spos.c:228:
+	if (ins == NULL)

Comparisons to NULL in the form (foo == NULL) or (foo != NULL)
are better written as (!foo) and (foo).

CHECK:ALLOC_SIZEOF_STRUCT: Prefer kmalloc(sizeof(*ins->modules)...) over kmalloc(sizeof(struct dsp_module_desc)...)
#73: FILE: sound/pci/cs46xx/dsp_spos.c:235:
+	ins->modules = kmalloc(sizeof(struct dsp_module_desc) * DSP_MAX_MODULES, GFP_KERNEL);

The allocation style is bad.  In general for family of
allocation functions using sizeof() to get memory size,
constructs like::

  p = alloc(sizeof(struct foo), ...)

should be::

  p = alloc(sizeof(*p), ...)

See: https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/process/coding-style.html#allocating-memory

